[48.644099, "o", "\u001b[34m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[34m──────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[34m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m Final Answer\u001b[0m\u001b[34m \u001b[0m\u001b[34m───────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[34m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m Based on the provided context, \u001b[1mNOODL\u001b[0m is a neurally plausible, provable online algorithm designed for machine         \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m learning applications with streaming data. It can be implemented as a three-layer neural network (comprising an      \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m input layer, a weighted residual evaluation layer, and a learning layer using Hebbian learning) and is applicable to \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m large-scale distributed learning tasks.                                                                              \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m It solves the problem of \u001b[1mexact recovery of both factors in the dictionary learning (DL) model\u001b[0m. In doing so, it       \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m eliminates the estimation bias incurred by prior dictionary estimation methods and achieves linear (geometric)       \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m│\u001b[0m convergence to the true factors.                                                                                     \u001b[34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[34m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
